{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791456275,"nonce":"QnuFLGe0CHqgmEFCsZ+MHzGG8YQ=","title":"Numeric class overrides disagree on vtable slot signatures","message":"Class-only scope of fb9da125afac67bb17c77bf4329bab6bd0f72f2a4ab4ee3ce11f51697879317f. Issue9836 calls an override taking Float through a parent taking Int and consumes an Int implementation result as Float. The original dispatcher used the implementation signature while the caller used its static type, producing stale floating-point values.\n\nNative Haxe preserves child.f(41.5) as 42.5; casting all calls through the introducing Int signature would lose the fractional argument. Class vtable slots now use F64 for I32/F32/F64 formals and results, converting at both the native method adapter and call site. Every Haxe Int is represented exactly. Erased I64 values, nullable scalars, Bool and references retain their representation. Class entries have a separate cache/name from native interface and iteration dispatch entries.\n\nImported method calls without local virtual_dispatch_info now consult the declaration index's stable slot layout. Native and pinned Cranelift fixtures cover local and imported parent/child calls, a separate reader module, multi-level overrides, negative values, Int limits, mixed String/Bool parameters and super calls.\n\nThe first full run exposed unannotated override formals lowered as Dynamic: BytesOutput.writeByte(c) differed from Output.writeByte(c:Int), breaking CrossModuleOverride and Issue5693. Unannotated override parameters now use the parent's registered signature, with builtin annotation fallback through the AST index. Body inference does not replace that contract; explicit variant annotations remain authoritative. Generic parent formals requiring substitution remain outside this inference path.\n\nValidation on the final implementation:\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check: exit 0 (/tmp/rayzor-variant-slo